dhcp: Build the resync throttler once

Since 2018 _periodic_resync_helper has built a new utils.throttler on
every pass, so each call got a fresh LockWithTimer with timestamp 0 and
never waited: resync_throttle has never throttled anything. Build the
throttled callable once in __init__ and reuse it in the loop.

A unit test drives two resync events 3 seconds apart with a 10 second
throttle and checks only the second one sleeps, for the remaining 7.

